\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces System architecture of the MMSAR evaluation framework. Visible RGB video streams are synthesized from text prompts using multimodal LLMs (Gemini 3.8 Flash and xAI Grok with resolution upscaling to $1280 \times 720$), followed by Melo thermal stylizing via a 256-level lookup table (\texttt  {melo\_lut}) to emulate pseudo-thermal infrared streams. The dual streams undergo dual-crop ($640 \times 640$) spatial extraction, video-level annotation in Label Studio, and 24~Hz frame extraction. Curated sequences are partitioned into 240-frame episodes under Option B (parent-video grouped split) with anti-adjacency snippet shuffling to eliminate cross-tile spatial leakage. At edge inference, parallel lightweight YOLO11n detectors process incoming RGB and thermal frames at 24~Hz ($T_s \approx 41.7$~ms), integrated via soft disjunctive late fusion ($s[n] = \max (c_{\text  {RGB}}[n], c_{\text  {Thermal}}[n])$) and evaluated across five lightweight temporal decision methods ($W = 5$ frames, 208~ms latency bound).}}{2}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:system_architecture}{{1}{2}{}{figure.1}{}}
